('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'inquiry-under-section-4-act', '297', 'Inquiry under section 4 of the Act, namely Sir Robert Owen;'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'c-minister-reference-secretary-state', '297', 'c. "the Minister" is a reference to the Secretary of State for the Home Department and, after the setting up of the Inquiry, to such other Government officials as are nominated by the Minister;'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'd-core-inquiry-team-reference', '297', 'd. "Core Inquiry Team" is a reference to the Chairman, counsel to the Inquiry, the solicitor to the Inquiry and such other persons as are agreed between the Minister and the Chairman and identified as such in writing;'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'e-hmg-advisers-reference-counsel', '297', 'e. "HMG advisers" is a reference to counsel and solicitors, instructed on behalf of Her'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'majesty-s-government-such-other', '297', 'Majesty''s Government, and such other Government officials as are nominated by the Minister;'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'f-relevant-witnesses-are-references', '297', 'f. "relevant witnesses" are references to witnesses whom the Chairman directs should be called to give evidence in a closed hearing as described in paragraphs');
INSERT INTO passages (report, section, paragraph_id, page, body) VALUES
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', '9-12-below-g-open', '297', '9 to 12 below; and g. "open rulings, judgments or reports" are references to rulings, judgments or reports produced by the Chairman in the course, or at the conclusion, of the'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'inquiry-which-may-be-released', '297', 'Inquiry which may be released to the public without risking harm to the public interest.'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'h-closed-hearings-are-hearings', '297', 'h. "Closed hearings" are hearings of the Inquiry to which paragraphs 9 to 14 below apply. This Restriction Notice is to be read as imposing no restriction on the disclosure of any document or information:'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'between-members-core-inquiry-team', '297', 'a. between members of the Core Inquiry Team for purposes connected with the'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'inquiry-b-minister-hmg-advisers', '297', 'Inquiry; or b. to the Minister or HMG advisers.'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'litvinenko-inquiry-107', '298', 'The Litvinenko Inquiry'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'restrictions-disclosure-publication-evidence-documents', '298', 'Restrictions on the Disclosure or Publication of Evidence or Documents given, produced or provided to the Inquiry 4 The restrictions referred to at paragraphs 5 and 7 below are imposed:'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'i-being-required-rule-law', '298', '(i) as being required by the rule of law known as public interest immunity; and/or'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'ii-because-minister-acting-accordance', '298', '(ii) because the Minister, acting in accordance with section 19(3)(b) of the Act'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'restrictions-attendance-inquiry-part-inquiry', '298', 'Restrictions on Attendance at the Inquiry or part of the Inquiry 8 The restrictions referred to at paragraphs 9, 12, and 14 below are imposed:'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'i-being-required-rule-law-2', '298', '(i) as being required by the rule of law known as public interest immunity; and/or'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'ii-because-minister-acting-accordance-2', '298', '(ii) because the Minister, acting in accordance with section 19(3)(b) of the Act'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'appendix-7-restriction-notices-orders-2', '299', 'Appendix 7 | Restriction Notices and Orders indicates in writing that the attendance of the person is necessary, and arrangements are in place which the Minister considers adequate to ensure that the public interest in preventing the disclosure of the Schedule material is not damaged. No person shall produce or show to any witness any of the Schedule material, or ask any questions which tend to reveal the existence or content of such material, otherwise than in accordance with a procedure formulated by the Core Inquiry Team and agreed in writing by the Minister. The Chairman shall ensure that no transcript of the evidence given at a closed hearing is made available to any person other than the Minister, members of the Core Inquiry Team or HMG advisers. The Chairman shall ensure that no reference is made to the substance of the evidence given at a closed hearing of the Inquiry in any open ruling, judgment or report arising out of the Inquiry, or otherwise.'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'G-BNWB)', 'amendments-restriction-notice-15-letter', '299', 'Amendments to this Restriction Notice 15 By letter to the Chairman under this paragraph the Minister may remove from the scope of this Notice any document or information referred to in the Schedule. The Chairman may invite the Minister to amend this Restriction Notice at any time upon providing the Minister with a draft of the proposed amendment and written reasons for it. The Minister may amend this Restriction Notice at any time. July 2014 (as amended 21 January 2015)'),
